From: AD5X Open OS
Subject: [PATCH] dma: ingenic: pdmam IRQ is optional on X2600

The X2600 PDMA node (13420000 and 13660000) has no "pdmam" interrupt; the
MCU mailbox IRQ belongs to the mcu node. The driver already treats pdmam as
optional (irq_pdmam < 0 is skipped), but platform_get_irq_byname() logs
"IRQ pdmam not found" on every probe. Use the _optional variant so the boot
log is clean. DMA behaviour is unchanged: pdma and pdmad are still requested.

--- a/module_drivers/drivers/dma/ingenic/ingenic_dma.c
+++ b/module_drivers/drivers/dma/ingenic/ingenic_dma.c
@@ -1170,7 +1170,7 @@
 	}
 
 	/* PDMA mcu interrupt*/
-	dma->irq_pdmam = platform_get_irq_byname(pdev, "pdmam");
+	dma->irq_pdmam = platform_get_irq_byname_optional(pdev, "pdmam");
 	if (dma->irq_pdmam >= 0) {
 		ret = devm_request_irq(&pdev->dev, dma->irq_pdmam, pdmam_int_handler,
 		                       0, "pdmam", dma);
